{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02717",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 4.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.78,
      "end_seconds": 11.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.9,
      "end_seconds": 18.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Yeah, it's weakness climbing up my legs. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.32,
      "end_seconds": 23.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.96,
      "end_seconds": 27.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "About... well, ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.21,
      "end_seconds": 30.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.46,
      "end_seconds": 49.82,
      "duration_seconds": 18.36,
      "text": "It usually comes with tingling in my feet. Mm, the tingling in my feet? That's been for about a month. Mm, with tingling in my feet, it's severe, honestly. Honestly, every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.24,
      "end_seconds": 61.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Did you notice any back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.7,
      "end_seconds": 65.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Nope, no back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.63,
      "end_seconds": 68.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Have you noticed bladder problems or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.77,
      "end_seconds": 74.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Okay, so no bladder problems or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.55,
      "end_seconds": 79.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.98,
      "end_seconds": 82.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.32,
      "end_seconds": 86.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.67,
      "end_seconds": 90.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.26,
      "end_seconds": 97.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Right, any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.32,
      "end_seconds": 101.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.06,
      "end_seconds": 109.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies. I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.09,
      "end_seconds": 113.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.44,
      "end_seconds": 117.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.58,
      "end_seconds": 123.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Glibenclamide. I take it 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.03,
      "end_seconds": 141.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.96,
      "end_seconds": 143.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.08,
      "end_seconds": 150.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.55,
      "end_seconds": 164.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.22,
      "end_seconds": 180.42,
      "duration_seconds": 14.2,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.92,
      "end_seconds": 183.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.09,
      "end_seconds": 185.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.47,
      "end_seconds": 190.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Okay, time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.58,
      "end_seconds": 202.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Right, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.46,
      "end_seconds": 231.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 110 over 82, SpO2 99 percent on room air, pulse 85, respiratory rate 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.64,
      "end_seconds": 237.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.72,
      "end_seconds": 240.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.62,
      "end_seconds": 245.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.89,
      "end_seconds": 261.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.5,
      "end_seconds": 264.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "So, raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.37,
      "end_seconds": 278.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Your ankle reflexes are absent and the strength in both legs is reduced."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.85,
      "end_seconds": 289.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Taking everything into account, it points towards possible Guillain-Barre syndrome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.36,
      "end_seconds": 293.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.31,
      "end_seconds": 323.31,
      "duration_seconds": 29.0,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now possible Guillain-Barre syndrome is my leading thought, not anything worse. An urgent admission is what I'd like next, for ascending weakness. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. We should do a lumbar puncture for possible GBS. You must be admitted today for monitoring of your breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.38,
      "end_seconds": 333.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.82,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.4,
      "end_seconds": 358.05,
      "duration_seconds": 24.65,
      "text": "Hm, okay. I'd like you to see the neurology team as well, and I'll write the referral. Let's hold off on a breathing test for now, and if there's no change in a month we can revisit it. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.6,
      "end_seconds": 362.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}